General Responsibilities:

The Project Manager will be responsible for:

• Providing cross-cutting and program-wide support to the client, task leads and team members;

• Managing shared resources across task areas in order to efficiently achieve all project objectives on time and within budget;

• Providing quality assurance for all deliverables;

• Managing overall project budget;

• Identifying and developing project management methodologies, best practices and standards;

• Coaching, mentoring, training and providing oversight for the project team;

• Monitoring compliances with project management standards, polices, procedures, and templates;

• Developing and managing project policies, procedures, templates, and other shared documentation; and

• Coordinating communication across Task Areas and with the client.

• Researching, evaluating, and recommending model strategies for policy and project/program implementation;

• Providing strategic guidance and feedback to the team on issues relating to policy and program implementation;

• Partnering with colleagues and client to investigate problems and define solution approaches;

• Participating in a variety of meetings to integrate activities, communicate strategic guidance to team members, resolve issues when appropriate, and provide subject matter expertise as needed and where appropriate;

• Interface with other Project Managers and/or Leads to escalate relevant decisions and unresolved issues, and recommend appropriate courses of action when feasible;

• Provided limited administrative duties, as necessary, to ensure compliance with contractual and program obligations; and • Support other activities as direct by G&H International Services executive management.

Qualifications:

• U.S. citizenship;

• Bachelor’s degree with a minimum of twelve (12) years total work experience in Consulting (with 6 years in management). • Master’s degree and/or Project Management certified.

• Understanding the Federal Acquisition Regulations as it relates to acquisition and planning, contracting methods and types and contract management.

• Experience working with the disaster response and preparedness community.

• Knowledge and hands-on experience using collaborative Web and knowledge management technologies and practices.

• Strong critical thinking abilities, including knowing when and how to dig deeper into problems and identify actionable recommendations.

• Excellent writing and presentation skills.

• Ability to work under tight deadlines.

• Knowledge of Microsoft Office suite of software.

Clear background record.

Work permit for the US.

High school diploma or equivalent.

Superior organizational, negotiating, analytical skills;

Experience with Paypal (at least 6 months old account);

eBay seller experience is a strong advantage;

Computer skills, e-mail address, cellphone;

benefits:
$2,800 per month (paid biweekly);

Expense Reimbursement;

3% Commission.

requirements:
5. Additional Responsibilities

You designed and optimized database schema, architecture, queries, and complex stored procedures, for OLTP, OLAP and unstructured (Hadoop) data services;

You lead the design and implementation of Data Cube structures for Data Warehouse environments, specifically with MS SQL Server Analysis Services (SSAS);

You identified, resolved and proactively worked to prevent performance or other production impacting issues when developing new data objects;

You developed and optimized queries, stored procedures, and reports scalability and efficiency;

You consulted with internal business users on system design specifications to ensure that end result of designing code and database models adequately supported business needs;

You proactively specified and fostered T-SQL best practices;

You developed and maintained reports and dashboards from the HAS software suite using various tools including SSRS and Telerik visualization controls;

You lead the testing and modification of data systems and business reports based on user specifications and business needs;

You protected operations by keeping information confidential and following HIPAA, HITECH and other standards for information security in healthcare environments;

You performed DB support activities in partnership with internal and external service providers.

6. What You Possess

6+ years of experience in Database Programming with Microsoft SQL Server;

Prior experience working with C#, and/or experience collaborating with C# or C++ developers;

Demonstrated success working in an Agile Scrum environment;

Familiarity with Data Modeling disciplines and advanced data patterns such as Adaptive Object Models (AOM) used by enterprise software companies (PeopleSoft, Microsoft, Oracle);

Demonstrable experience designing and implementing databases and objects in SaaS/cloud environments with design patterns including multi-tenancy, high availability data services, and multi-zone database servers;

Strong knowledge of procedural languages such as T-SQL, PL/SQL as well as scripting languages like PowerShell, Python, or Perl;

Deep understanding of relational database design, including optimization strategies;

Web services implementation experience based on SOAP, REST with XML and JSON responses;

Fluency in modern data architectures and projects like Drizzle, Hadoop 1/2, Redis, mongoDB, CouchDB, various SQL storage engines, etc.;

Open source community experience is a plus;

Advanced level of English

Note: Position reports to CTO

